[{"id":"comb-report-registers","itemId":"always-comb","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built <code class=\"nobreak\">mux4.sv</code>, whose <code class=\"nobreak\">always_comb</code> block is a 4-to-1 multiplexer, for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Slice Logic table of its Utilization report. A slice is one of the small groups of LUTs and flip-flops the chip is built from. The Slice Registers row counts the cells that remember a value; Used is how many this design takes.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the Used column of the Slice Registers row. <code class=\"nobreak\">always_comb</code> describes logic, worked out from the inputs as they are now, and every path through <code class=\"nobreak\">mux4</code>'s block gives <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> a value, so nothing has to remember anything: the multiplexer is a LUT and nothing else. Lesson 1.4 shows how an <code class=\"nobreak\">always_comb</code> block can end up with memory all the same.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/mux4/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":32,"excerpt":["+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","|        Site Type        | Used | Fixed | Prohibited | Available | Util% |","+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","| Slice LUTs              |    1 |     0 |          0 |     63400 | <0.01 |","|   LUT as Logic          |    1 |     0 |          0 |     63400 | <0.01 |","|   LUT as Memory         |    0 |     0 |          0 |     19000 |  0.00 |","| Slice Registers         |    0 |     0 |          0 |    126800 |  0.00 |","|   Register as Flip Flop |    0 |     0 |          0 |    126800 |  0.00 |","|   Register as Latch     |    0 |     0 |          0 |    126800 |  0.00 |","| F7 Muxes                |    0 |     0 |          0 |     31700 |  0.00 |","| F8 Muxes                |    0 |     0 |          0 |     15850 |  0.00 |","| Unique Control Sets     |    0 |       |          0 |     15850 |  0.00 |","+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+"],"ask":"How many cells that remember a value did Vivado use for mux4?","answer":"0","numeric":true},{"id":"comb-fill-default","itemId":"always-comb","role":"core","promptHtml":"Type the keyword that makes the last line of the <code class=\"nobreak\">case</code> cover every value of <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> that no line above lists.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">default</code> matches every value no other line names. In <code class=\"nobreak\">mux4</code> that is only 3, but with a <code class=\"nobreak\">default</code> the <code class=\"nobreak\">case</code> gives <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> a value whatever <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> is, so every path through the <code class=\"nobreak\">always_comb</code> block sets <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code>. Lesson 1.4 shows what happens when a path does not.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-01/mux4/mux4.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":18,"before":["// A 4-to-1 multiplexer: sel picks which of d0 to d3 reaches y.","module mux4 (","  input  logic [1:0] sel,","  input  logic       d0,","  input  logic       d1,","  input  logic       d2,","  input  logic       d3,","  output logic       y",");","  always_comb begin","    case (sel)","      2'd0:    y = d0;","      2'd1:    y = d1;","      2'd2:    y = d2;"],"blankLine":{"left":"      ","right":": y = d3;   // sel is 3: now every value of sel gives y a value"},"after":["    endcase","  end","endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// A 4-to-1 multiplexer: sel picks which of d0 to d3 reaches y.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"mux4","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false