lor":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" d3;   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// sel is 3: now every value of sel gives y a value","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}]},"after":[[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"endcase","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["default"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The missing keyword"},{"id":"comb-find-bug","itemId":"always-comb","role":"core","promptHtml":"This copy of lesson 1.3's <code class=\"nobreak\">mux4</code> should pick one of <code class=\"nobreak\">d0</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">d3</code> in an <code class=\"nobreak\">always_comb</code> block. Verilator warns COMBDLY about one of its lines. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>Inside <code class=\"nobreak\">always_comb</code>, every assignment uses <code class=\"nobreak\">=</code> (lesson 1.3). The line for <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 1 uses <code class=\"nobreak\">&lt;=</code>, which belongs to flip-flops (level 2), and Verilator warns about exactly that line. Synthesis would still build the same LUT, but in simulation a <code class=\"nobreak\">&lt;=</code> takes effect later than an <code class=\"nobreak\">=</code>, so the simulation and the hardware can disagree. Use <code class=\"nobreak\">=</code> on every line, as the other three do.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-01/comb_bug/comb_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// A 4-to-1 multiplexer: sel picks which of d0 to d3 reaches y.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"comb_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)"